        "raisedBy": [
          "accessibility"
        ],
        "recommendation": "Keyboard users (WCAG 2.1.2 No Keyboard Trap, 2.1.1 Keyboard). Once the menu is open, pressing Tab or Shift+Tab is cancelled and focus wraps among the four menu items, and the handler has no Escape branch, so the only way out is to activate an item, which also fires onChange. A keyboard user who opens the menu cannot Tab past it to the product list, nor dismiss it without picking an order. Per the APG menu-button pattern: on Escape, close the menu and return focus to the button; on Tab, do not preventDefault — close the menu and let focus move on naturally. Also close it when focus leaves the menu.\n",
